MARS Long Distance Replication Software
======================================

MARS provides asynchronous block storage replication through a Linux kernel
module, transaction logs and the marsadm administration tool. This fork
modernizes the out-of-tree module for unpatched Linux kernels, with x86-64
as the tested target. Other architectures and 64 KiB page sizes are unvalidated.

Start with INSTALL. Current support, replication/durability/discard semantics,
network configuration, release checks and remaining work are documented in
docu/modern-kernel.rst. The current guidance takes precedence over historic
kernel pre-patch requirements and roadmap promises in the original manual.

Build the module with the configured headers and compiler of the target
kernel. For Clang kernels:

    make -C kernel KDIR=/lib/modules/$(uname -r)/build LLVM=1 W=1

Build-tool regressions:

    python3 -m unittest discover -s test_suite/build -v

Disposable functional tests and their prerequisites are in
test_suite/qemu/README. CI configurations are in .github/workflows/.

Original project: https://github.com/schoebel/mars
Historical background: https://schoebel.github.io/mars/
The docu/ directory contains the original detailed administration manual.

